IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: CS (OS) No. 890 of 2008
CITATION: (2009) 9 SCC 797
YEAR: 2009

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Markandey Katju, Asok Kumar Ganguly

PARTIES:
Bajaj Auto vs TVS Motor Co

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Patents Act, 1970

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 108 Patents Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
twin spark plug patent, dts-i engine, expeditious patent trial, interim injunction

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Directed trial courts to hear patent infringement suits on a day-to-day basis and resolve matters within four months without lingering on interlocutory stages.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 108 Patents Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

